{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016UdG91KZdCda1sshKpaH24","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Current Evaluation State\n     2→\n     3→## Active Text\n     4→- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n     5→- **Attempt:** 4\n     6→- **Phase:** complete\n     7→- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n     8→- **final_score:** 8.80\n     9→\n    10→## Final Scores\n    11→- Structure Detection: 10/10\n    12→- Character Extraction: 8/10\n    13→- Character Profiles: 8/10\n    14→- Chapter Summaries: 10/10\n    15→- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10\n    16→- HTML Presentation: 9/10\n    17→- **Overall: 8.80/10** ✅ PASS (threshold: 8.0)\n    18→\n    19→## Evaluation Summary\n    20→\n    21→### What Worked Well\n    22→1. **Structure Detection (10/10):** Correctly identified as single short story (1 chapter)\n    23→2. **Chapter Summaries (10/10):** Comprehensive, accurate summary capturing all key events\n    24→3. **Character Extraction (8/10):** Both main characters (Fortunato, Montresor) correctly identified\n    25→4. **Character Profiles (8/10):** Rich profile for Fortunato; Montresor now has accurate narrator profile\n    26→5. **HTML Presentation (9/10):** Clean, modern design with functional navigation\n    27→\n    28→### Minor Issues (Not Blocking)\n    29→1. **Luchresi missing from character list** - 6-mention character filtered out, but appears in pronunciation guide\n    30→2. **Montresor has no evidence items** - Description is accurate but lacks supporting quotes\n    31→3. **Pronunciation false positives** - Some common English words flagged (jingled, filmy, orbs, leer)\n    32→4. **Latin word notes incorrect** - \"impune\" and \"lacessit\" have inaccurate definitions\n    33→5. **Medoc not flagged** - French wine region missing from pronunciation guide\n    34→\n    35→### Progress from Baseline\n    36→- **Baseline (Attempt 1):** 6.10\n    37→- **Attempt 3:** 7.70 (+1.60)\n    38→- **Attempt 4:** 8.80 (+2.70 total improvement)\n    39→\n    40→### Key Fixes That Worked\n    41→1. **Attempt 1:** Removed auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names; enhanced validation to reject objects/food/drink\n    42→2. **Attempt 2:** Fixed NER invalid name extraction (names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters)\n    43→3. **Attempt 3:** Added food/beverage filter (FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES set)\n    44→4. **Attempt 5/6:** Implemented narrator-aware profiling and fixed is_narrator field propagation\n    45→5. **Attempt 6:** Fixed plural family name extraction (\"Montresors\" rejected as family reference)\n    46→\n    47→## Fix History\n    48→\n    49→### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n    50→- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n    51→- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n    52→- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n    53→\n    54→### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n    55→- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n    56→- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n    57→\n    58→### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n    59→- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n    60→- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n    61→- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n    62→\n    63→### Attempt 4-5 (2026-01-18): Narrator-aware profiling\n    64→- Modified passage_gatherer.py to search for pronouns for narrator characters\n    65→- Modified pipeline.py to ensure narrator flag is set after identification\n    66→- Modified converter.py to boost mention_count for first-person narrators\n    67→- Modified analyzer.py to copy is_narrator and narrative_role to final Character object\n    68→- Modified analyzer.py to include narrators in profiling regardless of mention count\n    69→- Result: Montresor now has profile with is_narrator: true\n    70→\n    71→### Attempt 6 (2026-01-18): Fixed plural family name extraction\n    72→- Added possessive stripping logic in ner.py\n    73→- Added _is_plural_family_reference() method in validator.py\n    74→- Detects and rejects plural family names like \"Montresors\"\n    75→- Result: Analysis completes without LLM validation errors\n    76→\n    77→## Next Action\n    78→**Text complete!** Ready to advance to next text: `masque_of_red_death`\n    79→\n    80→---\n    81→\n    82→## Output Files\n    83→- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n    84→- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n    85→\n    86→## Pipeline Notes\n    87→- Analysis completed successfully in 7m 48s\n    88→- Pipeline processed 2,358 words\n    89→- Found 2 characters (Fortunato: 14 mentions, Montresor: 1 mention)\n    90→- Generated 2 character profiles\n    91→- Flagged 56 pronunciation words\n    92→- Low confidence noted for Montresor (due to first-person narration challenges)\n    93→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55fa45b0-2899-4135-b0e2-16de3c53baf7","uuid":"a04306cc-3ec6-491d-9fd6-adddfc8bcc3b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"# Current Evaluation State\n\n## Active Text\n- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n- **Attempt:** 4\n- **Phase:** complete\n- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n- **final_score:** 8.80\n\n## Final Scores\n- Structure Detection: 10/10\n- Character Extraction: 8/10\n- Character Profiles: 8/10\n- Chapter Summaries: 10/10\n- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10\n- HTML Presentation: 9/10\n- **Overall: 8.80/10** ✅ PASS (threshold: 8.0)\n\n## Evaluation Summary\n\n### What Worked Well\n1. **Structure Detection (10/10):** Correctly identified as single short story (1 chapter)\n2. **Chapter Summaries (10/10):** Comprehensive, accurate summary capturing all key events\n3. **Character Extraction (8/10):** Both main characters (Fortunato, Montresor) correctly identified\n4. **Character Profiles (8/10):** Rich profile for Fortunato; Montresor now has accurate narrator profile\n5. **HTML Presentation (9/10):** Clean, modern design with functional navigation\n\n### Minor Issues (Not Blocking)\n1. **Luchresi missing from character list** - 6-mention character filtered out, but appears in pronunciation guide\n2. **Montresor has no evidence items** - Description is accurate but lacks supporting quotes\n3. **Pronunciation false positives** - Some common English words flagged (jingled, filmy, orbs, leer)\n4. **Latin word notes incorrect** - \"impune\" and \"lacessit\" have inaccurate definitions\n5. **Medoc not flagged** - French wine region missing from pronunciation guide\n\n### Progress from Baseline\n- **Baseline (Attempt 1):** 6.10\n- **Attempt 3:** 7.70 (+1.60)\n- **Attempt 4:** 8.80 (+2.70 total improvement)\n\n### Key Fixes That Worked\n1. **Attempt 1:** Removed auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names; enhanced validation to reject objects/food/drink\n2. **Attempt 2:** Fixed NER invalid name extraction (names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters)\n3. **Attempt 3:** Added food/beverage filter (FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES set)\n4. **Attempt 5/6:** Implemented narrator-aware profiling and fixed is_narrator field propagation\n5. **Attempt 6:** Fixed plural family name extraction (\"Montresors\" rejected as family reference)\n\n## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n\n### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fixed NER invalid name extraction\n- Added check to reject names starting/ending with non-alphabetic characters\n- Result: Pipeline no longer fails on \"--yes\" from spaCy mis-tagging\n\n### Attempt 3 (2026-01-18): Added food/beverage filter\n- Added `FOOD_BEVERAGE_NAMES` set with 24 common food/drink terms\n- Pre-filter check before LLM validation\n- Result: Score improved 6.10 → 7.70 (+1.60 points)\n\n### Attempt 4-5 (2026-01-18): Narrator-aware profiling\n- Modified passage_gatherer.py to search for pronouns for narrator characters\n- Modified pipeline.py to ensure narrator flag is set after identification\n- Modified converter.py to boost mention_count for first-person narrators\n- Modified analyzer.py to copy is_narrator and narrative_role to final Character object\n- Modified analyzer.py to include narrators in profiling regardless of mention count\n- Result: Montresor now has profile with is_narrator: true\n\n### Attempt 6 (2026-01-18): Fixed plural family name extraction\n- Added possessive stripping logic in ner.py\n- Added _is_plural_family_reference() method in validator.py\n- Detects and rejects plural family names like \"Montresors\"\n- Result: Analysis completes without LLM validation errors\n\n## Next Action\n**Text complete!** Ready to advance to next text: `masque_of_red_death`\n\n---\n\n## Output Files\n- HTML: output/cask_of_amontillado/report.html\n- JSON: output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json\n\n## Pipeline Notes\n- Analysis completed successfully in 7m 48s\n- Pipeline processed 2,358 words\n- Found 2 characters (Fortunato: 14 mentions, Montresor: 1 mention)\n- Generated 2 character profiles\n- Flagged 56 pronunciation words\n- Low confidence noted for Montresor (due to first-person narration challenges)\n","numLines":93,"startLine":1,"totalLines":93}}}
